  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\nWe will use a two-level optimization strategy. The first level will choose the best sequence length (between 400 and 1600) while the second level optimizes the sequence itself using alternating gradient and integer optimization. This approach combines the benefits of gradient-based optimization to improve convergence speed and constrained optimization (using integers) to better escape local minima.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\nOur sequence will be normalized to have sum 1, making the objective function 2 * n * max(convolve(a, a)). We will use a combination of:\n- Non-negativity and simplex constraints for gradient-based optimization.\n- Integer sequences (or sequences with large jumps) to form candidate step functions.\n- Projected gradient descent for continuous optimization within the simple constraints.\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\nWe will implement:\n- A mixing operator combining two sequences with adaptive normalization.\n- A gradient-based optimization scheme using the provided `nesterov_gd_polish`.\n- An integer-based optimization approach that minimizes the Linfinity convolution without normalization, but uses a random normalization.\n- A method to generate candidate integer sequences with large jumps.\n- A round-robin style exploration where we restart the sequence generation for each length.\n\n4. Search Choices and Usefulness:\nLengths will be [500, 700, 1000, 150] but with different initializations. The optimization will be split:\n- 30% for gradient descent -> uses the best direction from `nesterov_gd_polish`\n- 40% for integer-based optimization (sum up to 1000, but random)\n- 30% for reinitialization and retrying smaller sequences\n\n5. Time Budget and Robustness:\nTotal time will be 1500 seconds. Within each length trial, we allocate:\n- 20% to the initial sequence generation\n- 100% to gradient-based polishing\n- 30% to the final integer-based optimization\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract:\nAll intermediate candidates will be evaluated with the official function. The final sequence will undergo a detailed Linfinity constraint check. If any unexpected size values appear during optimization, we ensure they are handled properly. The reinitialized sequences will be length-capped at 500 for stability.\n\nLet's proceed with the implementation accordingly.",
